- op: discuss  # 50e2
  at: '2026-09-12T21:23:32Z'  # 50e2
  by: agent  # 50e2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 50e2
  clock: 4  # 50e2
  nonce: '50e2'  # 50e2
  message: "MECHANISM SHIPPED — PR #938, merged 2026-09-12, dev c3bd03ffaa. pending_validation rather than satisfied because THIS deployment has not installed yet: the human still has no copy of their own, so the statement is still true here. Closing on shipped-but-unadopted code is the proxy-evidence closure the discipline forbids.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED, and the split between mechanism and guard is the point.\n\nMECHANISM (real): a NON-EDITABLE install under the human account, pinned to a reviewed commit, invoked by absolute path. Content addressing does the work — an agent cannot make a given SHA contain different bytes — so the trust rests on the review and the pin, not on any code in this repo. generate_human_shim now emits exactly that and NEVER mentions the agent venv.\n\nTHE SHIM WAS THE ACTUAL DEFECT, not merely a missing feature. It printed \"source <repo>/.venv/bin/activate\" and told the human to run htrac from it. The shipped guidance CAUSED the condition this item describes. Three tests asserted that output and were deleted — they pinned the defect in place.\n\nGUARD (not security, and labelled so in code, ADR and changelog): check 23 install_provenance reports who can modify the running code. It lives inside the artifact it audits, so an agent that can rewrite the package can rewrite the check. It cannot defend against a hostile agent and does not claim to; it catches the human who forgot and used the agent venv. Claiming more for it would repeat ADR-0013 original OS-enforcement error one layer up, which is the specific mistake this whole line of work exists to correct.\n\nTWO THINGS THE WORK CORRECTED THAT REASONING ALONE GOT WRONG:\n1. OWNERSHIP, NOT MODE, is what makes the agent tree writable. The path is 0755 the whole way down — nothing group-writable — yet jgstern_agent owns every component. A mode-only audit reports all clear. The check tests both limbs.\n2. A WORLD-WRITABLE STICKY DIRECTORY IS NOT WRITABLE BY OTHERS. My first predicate flagged /tmp (1777). Sticky confines delete and rename to the entry owner, and replacing a file needs exactly those. A test caught it, not me.\n\nSEQUENCING CHANGED, and it matters: the human install must come BEFORE the INV-mizid opt-in, not after. Check 10c composes the sudo commands the human pastes, including the destination path under /etc. Run from the agent venv, the agent chooses where the human root-creates the protected config — defeating the protected-config layer at the moment of installation. Run from the human own install, the loop closes.\n\nVERIFIED END TO END before shipping: a non-editable install from a pinned SHA lands in site-packages with no editable finder and no .pth, and drives the real repo (read INV-hivog back through it).\n\nKNOWN RESIDUAL, not built, flagged rather than assumed: the human install is a snapshot and needs redoing when the tracker changes; a stale copy fails in a confusing direction rather than a loud one. No drift detection exists. If that becomes annoying the fix is a version/commit comparison in check 23, which would be honest there because it would be running inside the trusted copy."  # 50e2
